        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/FF-resonance-header.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p>I think the most memorable bit of brilliance in the otherwise flawed diamond that is <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/games/final-fantasy-xvi\">Final Fantasy 16</a> is the way it handles legacy. There are moments where Clive and his recalcitrant band of revolutionaries rage against the way of the world: <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/games/2023/aug/18/final-fantasy-xvi-composer-masayoshi-soken\">they burn down cities, depose oligarchs, shatter crystals.</a> It's a none-too-subtle rallying cry against the binding nature of tradition: a radical plea to tear down the structures of the past in order to sow the seeds of the future.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/final-fantasy-resonance-review\">Read more</a></p>",
