        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/red-dead-redemption-2-horse_oWpviPa.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/it-really-does-look-like-rockstar-animated-horse-testicles-for-red-dead-redemption-2\">Red Dead Redemption 2's infamous animated horse testicles</a>, which are realistic enough to contract in cold weather and expand again in the warmth, were apparently not a feature mandated by Rockstar. As iconic as they've become -  a symbol of extraordinary detail in the game - they didn't originate from a list of features that needed to be added to the game. The horse testicles were instead the unexpected work of one person, or a group of people, autonomously working on the Cowboy epic.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/red-dead-redemption-2-horse-testicles-staff-autonomy-gta-6\">Read more</a></p>",
